; Tutorial_7_Read_a_PDF.inix -- read a PDF, scanned pages and all.
[about]
Title=7 - Read a PDF
Intro=A PDF of a scanned report becomes a Markdown document, and a Word document beside it.
Setup=HomerScribe is installed, with Ollama, Tesseract and Pandoc. A file named Annual_Report.pdf is in the Videos folder.
Homework=Give it a PDF with pictures in it. Each picture gets a description where it sits in the text.

[step]
Say=A scanned report came as a PDF with no text in it, just pictures of pages. HomerScribe reads the pages, recognises the text, describes any pictures, and writes a document.
Key=
Hear=

[step]
Say=Alt plus Control plus H. Then Alt plus B to browse.
Key=Alt+Control+H
Hear=HomerScribe dialog
Hear=Source paths: edit, https colon slash slash www dot youtube dot com slash watch question mark v equals 3 f 31 o u f q F S M

[step]
Say=Alt plus B.
Key=Alt+B
Hear=Choose a file to work on dialog
Hear=File name: edit

[step]
Say=Annual underscore Report dot p d f, Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=HomerScribe dialog
Hear=Source paths: edit, C colon backslash Users backslash Jamal backslash Videos backslash Annual Report dot p d f

[step]
Say=A PDF needs no box ticked: HomerScribe knows what to do with one. Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=HomerScribe, working
Hear=Preparing, Opening Annual Report dot p d f
Pause=1

[step]
Say=Preparing. It counts the pages and checks whether they carry text. These do not, so it reads them with Tesseract, page by page.
Key=
Hear=Reading, Page 12 of 40
Pause=1
Note=A PDF that already has text is read directly and is much quicker. Only scanned pages go through recognition.

[step]
Say=Page twelve of forty. Pictures on a page get described as it goes.
Key=
Hear=Describing, Page 15, a bar chart of revenue by region, five bars, the tallest labelled North America
Pause=1

[step]
Say=And the result.
Key=
Hear=Done. Annual Report dot p d f
Hear=HomerScribe results dialog
Hear=One source done. Took 11 minutes. Annual Report dot p d f: 40 pages read, 6 pictures described. C colon backslash Users backslash Jamal backslash Videos backslash Annual Report backslash Annual Report dot m d. Log of this run: C colon backslash Users backslash Jamal backslash Videos backslash Annual Report backslash HomerScribe dot log.
Hear=OK button
Pause=1

[step]

Say=A PDF whose pages carry text needs no recognition; it is read directly, which is much quicker.
Key=

[step]

Say=The check happens page by page, so a PDF that is part typed and part scanned is handled page by page as well.
Key=

[step]

Say=Recognition is done by Tesseract, on this computer, so a private document stays private.
Key=

[step]

Say=Pictures on a page are described by the same model that describes films, and the descriptions sit in the document where the pictures were.
Key=

[step]

Say=The Markdown document reads by heading in any editor or browser, and EdSharp's preview shows it formatted.
Key=

[step]

Say=The Word copy keeps the original's page breaks, so a page number someone mentions can still be found.
Key=

[step]

Say=The Word copy needs Pandoc, which the installer offers; without it, the Markdown document alone is written.
Key=

[step]

Say=A long report runs for a while; the window's title carries the page count, so Insert plus T checks on it.
Key=Insert+T
Hear=Page 12 of 40
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The folder can be zipped and shared with someone who needs the text, rather than the pictures of pages.
Key=

[step]

Say=The document's name follows the PDF's, so Annual Report dot p d f gives Annual Report dot m d, easy to find beside it.
Key=

[step]
Say=Forty pages and six pictures, eleven minutes. Enter. The folder holds Annual underscore Report dot m d, and, because Pandoc is installed, Annual underscore Report dot d o c x with the same page breaks as the original.
Key=Enter
Hear=HomerScribe dialog
Hear=Source paths: edit
Note=Without Pandoc, only the Markdown is written. The installer offers Pandoc as a box on its last page.
